# FurryOS live-build chroot environment overrides.
#
# Host constraint: /root/furryos is mounted nodev. Device nodes created on it
# exist but cannot be opened, which breaks every package postinst that
# redirects to /dev/null (base-files, dpkg, procps, libc6 ...).
#
# live-build's Chroot() helper enters the chroot with `env -i`, so anything
# exported by tools/lb.sh is wiped. Declaring the marker here re-establishes
# it for the second-stage debootstrap and every later chroot command, which
# then bind-mounts the host's working /dev devices instead of using the
# unusable nodes.
FURRYOS_BIND_DEVICES=1
